{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/25787-abducted-the-chosen","id":25787,"title":"Abducted: The Chosen?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-08T07:50:29-08:00","id":25787,"title":"Abducted: The Chosen?","content":"So Sikla Alkis and I were talking the other day, and for a little while now I've been thinking about a way to use aliens in WoD without resorting to the Cthulhu mythos. So, I decided that, why not <i>not</i> focus on the aliens, and instead focus on their mortal agents on Earth? And for another swerve, there's no overarching umbrella for each splat? Instead, each X-splat is constantly fighting each other, unlike the various covenants and lodges and stuff that have to grudgingly share the night. Already have some preliminary ideas for the five player factions.<br /> <br /> Mulloch: The red-eyed green warriors who exist to expand their empire, this time through the use of human proxies. Great fighters, but their chosen have such a one-track mind that social skills are non-existent. Their bases are in their saucer-shaped craft, and the primary focus of their mutations is on a human's physical and mental abilities.<br /> Recticulan: The classic gray alien, small bodied, big eyed, and utterly focused on finding out everything they can about everything. They specialize in everything knowledgeable, but their chosen are so reliant on technology that their physicality is laughable. Their bases are their flying wing ships.<br /> Reptoids: David Icke's wet dream/nightmare, the Reptoids have been on Earth for centuries. Though they aren't nearly as in control as they like to brag, they still have the ability to grant their chosen great psychic powers and social boons, but without physical skills to accompany. They base themselves in cigar-shaped craft, often underwater.<br /> Locusts: A race without a name, the chosen of the Locusts are utterly focused on scouting out Earth's resources for the eventual invasion. These chosen are often mentally broken, but also ready to do what they must, meaning that there are few penalties for morality loss. The Locusts base themselves out of techno-organic craft.<br /> Aes: Old gods of mankind, having left the people of Earth after discovering that there are other worlds between worlds. Their chosen have been instructed to protect and guide mankind, but with a strange morality that, while helping their psychical and social skills, has left their long term planning to suffer. The Aes chosen often congregate in runic craft that vaguely resemble ancient chariots.<br /> <br /> The Greater Collective: A group of races that have been brought together by force so that no one can ever be alone again. The Collective wants to absorb all life to become whole, and so never be a single useless entity. The other races combat it with gusto, but the Collective knows it is better than to be a single part in a mismatched whole. Collective chosen have access to each others skills, but their traits are still their own.<br /> <br /> Anomalies: Miniature black holes, warps in space-time, tears into quantum reality, etc. The truth is that the universe has some weird shit going on in it. There's plenty of theories on how it all happens, but until someone can get a better idea, all the chosen can do is try and repair what's been damaged like a kind of planetary janitor staff.<br /> <br /> Theme: Struggling Apart: None of the alien races like each other, and as such their chosen don't either. Unlike mage orders or werewolf packs, it's almost open war sometimes between the chosen of two different alien races.<br /> <br /> Mood: Lonliness: Unlike every other splat, the chosen are often forced to work solo, never having the companionship of someone who can at least understand what it's like to suddenly be grabbed out of your bed and turned into something else. Add in that four out of the five races care nothing for humanity, and the fifth has a touch of blue and orange morality, and you're very much alone.<br /> <br /> Again, this is supposed to be getting the idea of aliens <i>away</i> from the Cthulhu mythos for a while, so what do you guys think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T14:59:35-08:00","id":26068,"title":"","content":"While you're trying to avoid the Cthulhu Mythos, I would look to the Rejections we developed for Outsider: the Calling. A Google search should bring you to the blog with a link to the google doc. I look forward to seeing what comes of this, as I'm eager to drag in some Greys to my WoD without it seeming forced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T21:35:08-08:00","id":26290,"title":"","content":"Don't believe him! He works for them, the shadow government.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T22:43:54-08:00","id":26313,"title":"","content":"Don't try and threaten me, Demo, I've watched presidents die. *Smokes*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T08:52:13-08:00","id":26542,"title":"","content":"How many did you kill?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T16:19:52-08:00","id":26797,"title":"","content":"*Thinks* Carry the three...<br /> <br /> But back to topic, Sikla and I felt &quot;Plasma&quot; would be a good power/resource, but we can't seem to agree on how to gather it. Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T22:17:19-08:00","id":27000,"title":"","content":"Plasma could go either way. Been doing more 40k gaming so I see where your going, but the Vampire fans might interpret it as blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T02:17:23-08:00","id":27072,"title":"","content":"I'd take a step back Flyboy. Come up with the core theme and mood (and how this is different from Changeling) before you worry about splats and traits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T04:01:07-08:00","id":27878,"title":"","content":"Yeah, like why would someone work for the people they abducted them? They are brainslaves or something? Players may not enjoy playing slaves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T20:34:08-08:00","id":30729,"title":"","content":"Yeah there ought to be groups who work for the aliens, those who oppose the aliens, those who want to negotiate with the aliens, and those who want to take the aliens for all their worth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T05:39:03-08:00","id":30915,"title":"","content":"I'd actually love to see a book based on Abducties, but in all honesty I would suggest reading some more lore. One of the things that really makes alien abduction good or intriguing in fiction is not the feeling of loneliness or struggling idiologies but instead the mixed feeling of abandonment and violation. I would love to see this developed though, the ideas are a good jumping point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1275-solusxisle","name":"SolusXisle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T07:30:03-08:00","id":30959,"title":"","content":"This discussion makes me want a blue book on aliens. They're one of the few antagonists almost completely untouched on, other than in one piece of Hunter fiction and as a &quot;maybe a True Fae could be them I guess&quot; nod in Changeling core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T08:58:43-08:00","id":31009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/25787-abducted-the-chosen?p=30959#post30959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This discussion makes me want a blue book on aliens. They're one of the few antagonists almost completely untouched on, other than in one piece of Hunter fiction and as a &quot;maybe a True Fae could be them I guess&quot; nod in Changeling core.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a little more than a nod in the Horror Recognition Guide's SASs (Collection of Horrors)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1275-solusxisle","name":"SolusXisle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T18:49:20-08:00","id":31401,"title":"","content":"I do like themes of violation, but abandonment is a more powerful one, and can help separate this from Changeling even more. Sure, some were just left to be lost by their keepers, but the changelings never really <i>feel</i> abandoned. The abducted, I'm thinking, are lucky to see the things that made them once every few years.<br /> <br /> Also, everyone knows where these different alien types were drawn from right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T19:09:40-08:00","id":31414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/25787-abducted-the-chosen?p=30959#post30959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This discussion makes me want a blue book on aliens. They're one of the few antagonists almost completely untouched on, other than in one piece of Hunter fiction and as a &quot;maybe a True Fae could be them I guess&quot; nod in Changeling core.</div> </div> </div> </div>The <i>Changeling</i> aspect is a bit more explicit than that: the core flat-out states that some, although not necessarily all, of alien sightings <i>are</i> Fae, and the Greys are one of the actual examples later on. It's just that they are ultraterrestrial rather than extraterrestrial.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">(Previously known by the name of &quot;GrimGent&quot;.)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/335-the-yann-waters","name":"The Yann Waters","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T21:26:53-08:00","id":31454,"title":"","content":"And the Greys are mage cryptids and the reptilians are demon cryptids and the the reptilians, grey, and nordics are all alien races in infinite macabre. <br /> <br /> But mothman is both a demon cryptid and a promethean, so there are being more than one explanation for something is hardly new to the world of darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T22:14:10-08:00","id":43352,"title":"","content":"So I've gotten some thinking about this, and feel that the theme of violation and mood of abandonment/lonlieness works for these types of characters. As for why the abducted will work with the aliens, I'm wondering if each alien species has a method of control for each abducted, without completely suppressing the chosen's personality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T05:11:30-08:00","id":43449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/25787-abducted-the-chosen?p=43352#post43352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I've gotten some thinking about this, and feel that the theme of violation and mood of abandonment/lonlieness works for these types of characters. As for why the abducted will work with the aliens, I'm wondering if each alien species has a method of control for each abducted, without completely suppressing the chosen's personality.</div> </div> </div> </div>That piques my interest. DaveB had a character who was capable of erasing the memory of player characters. Therefore he would roll the NPC's mind wiping ahead of time, and play through the scene, skipping the parts that would be erased.<br /> <br /> I imagine you could come up with some pretty interesting meta-mechanics for mind control and make a challenge out of having the players figure out what they've been doing while under the influence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T08:18:04-08:00","id":1156058,"title":"","content":"ARISE, MY CREATION, ARISE!!!<br /> <br /> So I had some time to dwell on this one for quite a time, and I had a few new ideas that might work to make this game stand more on it's own.<br /> <br /> 1: People mentioned that there needed to be a reason that the abducted would be working for the aliens, and on introspection I think that's the key; they <i>aren't</i>. Or at least, not all of the abducted are. Those taken by the Mulloch, the Reticulans, and the Saurians (Renaming because Demon has Reptilians now) are just trying to play along for their own ends, or actually <i>are</i> working for the aliens as collaborators. The Locust chosen have no way to play along because of the brain parasite, and the Aes aren't working against their gods, but they aren't sure working with them is a good idea either.<br /> <br /> 2: Reading up some more on abduction myth, I think that for the aliens to be so interested in Earth, the paranormal is a good draw as anything mankind does. The Mulloch might be confused as to why we're so merciful to those we &quot;conquer&quot;, and how we're crazy enough to nuke &quot;valuable resources&quot; into oblivion, but to the Reticulans it's amazing how we don't utilize &quot;vast energy resources&quot; (Supernal Energy, Sekhem, Pyros). Basically, Earth's got some crazy shit on it, and the aliens can use it.<br /> <br /> So, what else do you guys think can be done to try and bring this one up to standards?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T12:22:56-08:00","id":1156116,"title":"","content":"First, do a Doc. Or anything else that keeps the project from simply drowning in the forums.<br /> <br /> I like the idea, but I think it is time to drop the premise of open warfare, thought it might be implicit in your current scheme. Abductees are likely to search for others that went through the same experience, though some can never find anything beyond nutjobs who think they were abducted. Some could even find the Changelings that way, and maybe some kinship with them, so it could be interesting to consider their crossover possibilities in particular.<br /> <br /> As something to differentiate them, though, we need something to reinforce the themes of abandonment. The Changelings were violated, but they can easily find their common ground behind the seemingly diverse transformation, and they share the experience of the Hedge and Arcadia. Abductees should have something in their experience that sets them apart even from each other. Each was a specific experiment, each was a messing with humanity, and each were thrown away later, either to be observed, used or simply was discarded. Even the victims of the same species should find little in common. They weren't meant to.<br /> <br /> The sense of violation specific for Abductees probably would be better served with almost complete loss of contact with their &quot;creators&quot;. Even if they come again, every time is the same. The aliens don't want company or service, they don't see their victims as allies. They come and capture the same Abductee again, experiment and record, and leave exactly as they did before. Maybe other species can find it on their interest to contact those victims as allies and as a source of information on the activities of others. But the ones responsible for your existence as what you are now don't care. You are nothing to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T13:05:02-08:00","id":1156143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/25787-abducted-the-chosen?p=1156116#post1156116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, do a Doc. Or anything else that keeps the project from simply drowning in the forums.<br /> <br /> I like the idea, but I think it is time to drop the premise of open warfare, thought it might be implicit in your current scheme. Abductees are likely to search for others that went through the same experience, though some can never find anything beyond nutjobs who think they were abducted. Some could even find the Changelings that way, and maybe some kinship with them, so it could be interesting to consider their crossover possibilities in particular.<br /> <br /> As something to differentiate them, though, we need something to reinforce the themes of abandonment. The Changelings were violated, but they can easily find their common ground behind the seemingly diverse transformation, and they share the experience of the Hedge and Arcadia. Abductees should have something in their experience that sets them apart even from each other. Each was a specific experiment, each was a messing with humanity, and each were thrown away later, either to be observed, used or simply was discarded. Even the victims of the same species should find little in common. They weren't meant to.<br /> <br /> The sense of violation specific for Abductees probably would be better served with almost complete loss of contact with their &quot;creators&quot;. Even if they come again, every time is the same. The aliens don't want company or service, they don't see their victims as allies. They come and capture the same Abductee again, experiment and record, and leave exactly as they did before. Maybe other species can find it on their interest to contact those victims as allies and as a source of information on the activities of others. But the ones responsible for your existence as what you are now don't care. You are nothing to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds pretty close to Deviant (from what we know so far). I don't know if that is a positive, or a sign that more differentiation is needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reac